    "snapshot_alignment": "nocache_d0 cycles sum 17,971,370 matches P-SNAPSHOT 14-workload total 17,971,370",
    "main_findings": [
      "Delay-0 cache configs do not reduce cycles; I-L1 neutral, D-L1 and I+D+L1/L2 increase cycles on common 13-workload subset.",
      "I-L1, D-L1, and L2 substantially reduce arb/RAM transactions (often 10x-20x), but single-outstanding pipeline cannot convert traffic reduction into IPC.",
      "Memory-heavy workloads (mem_seq/mem_ldst/mem_random) show the largest stall/cycle sensitivity; mem_random times out with D-L1 or L2 at 5M cycles.",
      "Memory delay mode 1 and 2 greatly increase cycle counts and cause timeouts; full cache does not recover the added latency for mem_seq/mem_random.",
      "Recommendation: prioritize F3 (bounded outstanding/MSHR/store buffer) for memory-heavy; keep F1 as front-end prerequisite; do not prioritize cache capacity/strategy work on this baseline."
    ]
  },
